# THE SIGN-OFF LEDGER — NEVER COMMITTED.
#
# Who approved each procedural entry, and when. The supervising lawyer is a named private
# individual, and this repository is PUBLIC: anything committed here is published, in the
# history, permanently. The build has no use for it either — `data/index.json` ships inside
# a public JS bundle, so a name in the frontmatter would be downloadable by every visitor.
#
# So the ledger lives on the owner's machine only. `data-check` reads it when it is there and
# reports the sign-off count; without it the count simply reads 0, which is the honest answer
# for a clone that holds no record. `data/approvals.example.json` shows the shape.
data/approvals.local.json
